# Thrun's targeting restriction stops only nongreen spells and abilities its controller's opponents control (CR 601.2c),
# and "During your turn, Thrun has indestructible" (CR 702.12b) holds only on its controller's turn. On turn 3 Bot1 aims its
# own Lightning Bolt (red) at Thrun: its controller is no opponent, so the target is legal and Thrun takes 3. Still on
# Bot1's turn, Bot2's Assassin's Trophy - black and green, so not nongreen - targets Thrun, which is indestructible and
# survives (Bot1 declines the basic land). On turn 4, Bot2's turn, Thrun has no indestructible: Giant Growth (green)
# targets it (8/8), and a second Assassin's Trophy destroys it.

